failure_location.quote:
Let $\wsm$ be any first order stationary point attained by \mkl.
	Under assumptions 1-3, for a given $\epsilon <1$ and $\lambda$ as defined in equation \eqref{eq:lambdasc}, there exists a $k'$ such that for all $k \geq k'$,
	\begin{align*}
		\norm{\wsm -\ws}  \leq \dfrac{\epsilon^k G}{\lambda}
	\end{align*}

